# Split Button — a "Start" chip that splits into two chips (Google left, Apple
# right) with springs on translateX/padding and FadeIn/FadeOut layout content;
# either chip collapses it back to "Start".
# What this test covers: split via Start, collapse via the left (Google) chip,
# split again and collapse via the right (Apple) chip, rapid toggles on the
# right chip while its spring is still moving (x=240 is on the right chip in
# both states), and hitting the left chip while it is still sliding out.
context platform=ios
open "demos://animations/split-button"
wait "label=\"Close\"" 45000
# Warm-up touch on the status bar: the first touch of a test can be lost while
# the XCTest runner attaches.
press 330 20
wait 500
wait "text" "Start" 10000
wait 800
press "label=\"Start\""
wait 1000
# Left (Google) chip collapses the split.
press 128 437
wait 1000
wait "label=\"Start\"" 3000
press "label=\"Start\""
wait 1000
# Right (Apple) chip collapses it too.
press 274 437
wait 1000
wait "label=\"Start\"" 3000
# Rapid toggles interrupting the springs + FadeIn/FadeOut layout animations.
press 240 437 --count 4 --interval-ms 200
wait 1500
press 240 437 --count 6 --interval-ms 90
wait 1500
# Split and immediately hit the left chip while it is still sliding out.
wait "label=\"Start\"" 3000
press "label=\"Start\""
wait 300
press 128 437
wait 1200
wait "label=\"Start\"" 3000
wait "label=\"Close\"" 15000
press "role=\"button\" label=\"Close\""
wait 1500
